.page paste 1 merge lines of files side by side

# SYNOPSIS
*paste* [*-s*] [*-d* _LIST_] [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`paste` writes lines that consist of the corresponding lines of each _FILE_ joined by a tab. A file name of `-` stands for standard input; with no file `paste` reads standard input. When one file runs out its column is left empty.

# OPTIONS
@ *-d* _LIST_
    Use the characters of _LIST_, one after another and cycling, instead of tabs as separators.
@ *-s*
    Serial: paste all the lines of one file into one output line, then do the same for the next file.

# EXAMPLES
    paste names.txt scores.txt
    seq 1 4 | paste -s -d,
    paste -d: users.txt homes.txt

# SEE ALSO
cut(1), sort(1), tr(1)
